-- Overview --
Survata is democratizing the multi-billion dollar market research industry by making it easy and affordable for anyone to survey a target population (e.g., to ask 100 women in Oregon about grocery shopping habits). We gather responses through a unique means – the surveywall, in which respondents answer surveys on publisher sites across the web in exchange for premium content. We are a small, well-funded team based in the beautiful Bay Area. Our founders have been friends since childhood (almost 25 years) and aim to operate the team as a group of friends tackling fun challenges.<p>-- Position: full stack engineer --
We are seeking a full stack software engineer to lead the development of our surveywall interview system. On the client side, you will build a top tier third party JavaScript library that provides pan-browser and pan-device support for dozens of publisher websites while guaranteeing minimal performance impact and a quality user experience, even in the face of downtime or heavy load on the Survata servers. On the server side, you will tackle the interesting conceptual challenge of determining when a respondent is answering honestly. And you will help build a classifier to categorize answers as honest or not.<p>Required skills:
* JavaScript;
* Python;
* SQL;
* Unix script<p>Desired skills:
* client-side MVC framework; 
* third party JavaScript widgets;
* web performance optimization;
* Amazon Web Services;
* machine learning (namely supervised classifiers)<p>-- How to apply --
Survata offers competitive salary, equity, health care, and other benefits. Most importantly, we offer challenging problems, independence, and the opportunity to learn and grow.  We are looking for friendly, talented individuals to join the team.  Send a resume, LinkedIn&#x2F;Github profile, and&#x2F;or a link to an interesting web app that you&#x27;ve built to jobs@survata.com.

